{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118256","id":3494825625,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7QTs6Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118256","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118256.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118256.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118256","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118256/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118256/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118256/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f5e23ae470fdfc44c5b7ba9035181778313a2d73","number":118256,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Extend output filtering functionality and improve UX","user":{"login":"mFieldHouses","id":131540025,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9ckOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131540025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses","html_url":"https://github.com/mFieldHouses","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The editor output text filtering system has been, at least in my experience, pretty horrid. It just removes any message not containing a match with your query text, making it pretty useless since there's no context visible around messages that match the query text.\r\n\r\nI have made a few small changes to output filtering to make the experience of trying to find certain strings in the output log a bit smoother. These changes/additions are:\r\n\r\n - Option to show lines that do not contain the target string via a toggle button (Visible to the left of the clear output button). This option is enabled by default.\r\n - Toggle button for case-sensitivity\r\n - Highlighting of the target string inside of the lines that contain the target string.\r\n - Scroll position retention\r\n - Integration with message type filters\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b472ef7-fee1-4775-87e6-81cdc0d9f305\">\r\n\r\nA nice side effect that has come with my changes is that updating the log when searching for something is not choppy anymore. You may have noticed that when you changed the search query, there's a bit of very short flickering before you get your results. I accidentally fixed that in my attempts to get scroll position retention working. The fix was calling `log->set_scroll_follow(false)` before calling `_rebuild_log()`. (And then, of course, reverting with `log->set_scroll_follow(true)` afterwards)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic: